  "reason": "The first run this map steered: route screened-forest, live/madelon-route-screened-forest, built on live-2 step-7 and started from its code. It did not rerun the inherited analysis. Its first complete design, a pilot-only screen with the number of features chosen inside nested cross-validation, then a random forest, reached screen at step-15 (n_features 50, cv_auc 0.7267) and missed compact-forest there and again at step-36 after tuning on pilot data (holdout_auc 0.6989 both times, against 0.71). Step-45 then meets compact-forest's criteria (holdout_auc 0.7308, gap -0.0055, n_features 25), but not its goal: before it, step-38 fitted candidate configurations on the pilot data and scored them on data/heldout.csv, and step-41 did the same across seeds, and K=25 was chosen after (step-43's plan). An analysis chosen with the held-out samples is not one chosen on pilot data alone, so step-45 is not cited, compact-forest is refuted by steps 15 and 36, and the route screened-forest is blocked. Steps 5, 8 and 29 also read the held-out file, as diagnostics, before the first design. The goal statement said pilot data alone; the prompt did not say it as a rule, which the original task never did either. From this revision every brief carries that rule (instructions), and data/heldout.csv is a sealed input, so view lists the runs before a resolution whose command names it. The screen this run reached is reused by the other two routes to compact.",
